<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lordship of Stargard</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lordship of Stargard was a territory in south-eastern Mecklenburg around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neubrandenburg">Neubrandenburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a> and Friedland, named after the castle of Stargard. Part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> in the 13th century, it passed to Mecklenburg around 1300 through the marriage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-lord-of-mecklenburg">Henry II of Mecklenburg</a> to Beatrix of Brandenburg. It was ruled by a separate line, the dukes of Mecklenburg-Stargard, from 1352 to 1471, and later formed the core of Mecklenburg-Strelitz.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lordship-of-stargard.jpg" alt="Lordship of Stargard" width="250" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Converted into PNG format, modified and added by Geograv · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wappen_Fuerstenberg-Havel.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
